adjudication.rationale:
Yes. In `addGuests.handler.ts`, the authorization explicitly treats any existing attendee as authorized to perform the `addGuests` mutation:

```ts
const isAttendee = !!booking.attendees.find((attendee) => attendee.email === user.email);

if (!isTeamAdminOrOwner && !isOrganizer && !isAttendee) {
  throw new TRPCError({ code: "FORBIDDEN", ... });
}
```

This means a user who is merely an attendee on the booking (not organizer/admin/owner) can add additional guest emails to that booking (subject only to blacklist and “not already an attendee” checks). That is a real, verifiable privilege grant in the diff and can be a security/correctness issue if attendees were only supposed to have read access.
